with drafts as (
  select value as item from jsonb_array_elements($explainer_drafts$[{"id":"7ba33217-114f-5014-abc4-f2c2529eb91b","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What is a union, and what does it do for me?","body":"A union is an organization of workers. Massachusetts public-sector law (M.G.L. c. 150E) calls it an \"employee organization\" that helps its members improve their wages, hours and working conditions. When a union is the exclusive representative of your bargaining unit, it negotiates the contract that covers everyone in the unit. It must also represent the interests of all employees in the unit without discrimination, whether or not they are members. In a union workplace, grievances usually follow a set procedure that the union tracks.","attribution":"","source":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: grievance, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 5, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section5); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 1, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section1)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","membership"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":fals