fbbc5d6b424aac107445ef5fed5e792fd59f0e2b96b3b87f0063b696b1af5228","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"eb9e0837-d116-5ced-a013-3100452961eb","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Qué es un delegado o delegada sindical?","body":"Un delegado o delegada sindical (steward) es un representante del sindicato. La ley laboral federal incluye al \"shop steward\" entre los representantes del sindicato, junto con sus funcionarios y agentes. Para los trabajadores del sector privado cubiertos por la National Labor Relations Act, la Junta Nacional de Relaciones Laborales (National Labor Relations Board, NLRB) dice que el representante que usted pida en una entrevista de investigación puede ser un delegado sindical, un agente, un funcionario del sindicato o un compañero de trabajo. En el empleo público de Massachusetts, el sindicato tiene derecho a reunirse con los empleados en el trabajo durante el día para investigar y hablar sobre quejas formales (grievances) y otros asuntos laborales. La forma de elegir a los delegados la fijan las reglas propias del sindicato, que los sindicatos cubiertos por la ley federal de informes deben describir en sus declaraciones.","attribution":"","source":"National Labor Relations Board (nlrb.gov), Weingarten Rights, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.nlrb.gov/about-nlrb/rights-we-protect/your-rights/weingarten-rights); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 402 - Definitions (LMRDA), consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/402); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 5A, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section5A); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 431 - Report of labor organizations, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/431)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","membership"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-is-a-steward","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-25da50f7964da3cf38223933a4538061b435fafbb7cb961aac5f533010654630","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-is-a-steward","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What is a steward?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"d7da95f81227d3b02a00cd2c346e27a2a1626f5e40b35083eb56392bafc74c2a","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-c0c297b8befc2b93310f26c155213d827e18c3f0f1247935f02f3d1aed299f0d","prov-30e45a7bc7e1b4b3b3cba47cc0bcd2be7f99e80d204c2ea66b47b674a1a1af5e","prov-26ecba5c6cbc9ab17124be4fa65f69f9729091fb7a55b2df07dddb222a07b830","prov-c7bfdf0c8b0ca70089e10fd447440bd95248d9e1