u/uscode/text/29/431","publisher":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu)","title":"29 U.S. Code 431 - Report of labor organizations","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:05:57Z","content_sha256":"fbbc5d6b424aac107445ef5fed5e792fd59f0e2b96b3b87f0063b696b1af5228","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"77f7b965-385a-59e8-a00c-d319a57c5b3e","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Quién decide lo que mi sindicato pide en la negociación?","body":"En el empleo público de Massachusetts, el sindicato que es el representante exclusivo negocia con el empleador sobre salarios, horarios, normas de productividad y desempeño, y otros términos y condiciones de empleo. Cada parte puede elegir quién la representa en la mesa de negociación. La forma en que el sindicato fija sus demandas la deciden su constitución y sus estatutos. Los sindicatos cubiertos por la ley federal de informes deben presentar una declaración ante el Departamento de Trabajo de EE. UU. que explique cómo se autorizan las demandas de negociación y cómo se ratifican los términos del contrato. La ley federal también da a los miembros de esos sindicatos el derecho de asistir a las reuniones de miembros y participar en el debate y la votación.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - The Collective Bargaining Process, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-the-collective-bargaining-process); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 6, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section6); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 411 - Bill of rights; constitution and bylaws of labor organizations, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/411); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 431 - Report of labor organizations, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/431)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","membership"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-who-decides-what-the-union-negotiates","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-69853fad086bff8efcae0447edded48dcb93f71dfa30715b8d6f8c0f442c6332","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-who-decides-what-the-union-negotiates","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"Who decides what my union asks for in bargaining?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"5c41e9ca35aa727ca5fed07ecffb148ca263f29e9d6811370466301f8c9370a0","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8f25653210c21b4f2f69e663cae59958