nts to stop. The DLR also says you may ask about filing a non-payment of wage complaint with the Fair Labor Division of the Massachusetts Attorney General's Office. Keep copies of your notice, the authorization you signed, and your pay stubs. The DLR guidance is about agency fees after Janus. If you are a member who signed a dues authorization, its revocation terms under M.G.L. c. 180, s. 17A also matter, so ask your steward or union office to review it with you.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 180, section 17A, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXII/Chapter180/Section17A); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), DLR Q&A re: Janus v. AFSCME, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/dlr-qa-re-janus-v-american-fed-of-state-cty-muni-employees)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","dues"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-money-still-taken-after-i-stopped","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-260216c014acc319ec8d04c70156118570165bbe1880554c404b0ebb2a2b1e10","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-money-still-taken-after-i-stopped","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"I asked to stop paying, but money is still taken from my check. Wh