nd":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What does \"just cause\" mean for discipline?","body":"Just cause asks whether an employer had a good reason to fire or discipline an employee. It contrasts with employment at will, the default rule in which a job can be ended by either side at any time and for almost any reason. In Massachusetts, the civil service law says a tenured civil service employee may not be discharged, removed or suspended for more than five days except for just cause and after the steps the law requires. Your contract may also set its own discipline standard, so read your contract and ask your steward how just cause is applied in your workplace.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 31, section 41, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleIV/Chapter31/Section41); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: just cause, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/just_cause); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: employment-at-will doctrine, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/employment-at-will_doctrine)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","rights-at-work"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"fa