record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"6ddf6781-f442-5cdb-afaa-99b96ae3680b","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Quién puede presentar una queja formal? ¿Puedo presentarla yo mismo?","body":"Las quejas formales las puede presentar un empleado o un grupo. En el empleo público de Massachusetts, la ley c. 150E, sección 5, dice que usted puede presentar una queja formal a su empleador y que se escuche sin intervención del sindicato, siempre que el sindicato tenga la oportunidad de estar presente en esas reuniones y que cualquier arreglo sea compatible con el contrato vigente. Llevar una queja a arbitraje (arbitration) ante el Departamento de Relaciones Laborales (DLR) es distinto: el DLR dice que un empleador, una organización de empleados o ambos pueden pedir que se inicie el arbitraje de quejas. El procedimiento de su contrato también importa, así que hable con su delegado o delegada sindical antes de decidir.","attribution":"","source":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: grievance, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 5, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section5); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), File a petition for arbitration, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/file-a-petition-for-arbitration)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-can-i-present-a-grievance-myself","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-7f92a866999d4c85d25af335aaba4c9220e45dda558417dfcb6def817b81f8ce","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-can-i-present-a-grievance-myself","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"Who can file a grievance? Can I present one myself?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"c96207796901ba60178d8b33eb80814abe1f6f2b7c0c332726c1dc5fb0809965","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","prov-5d64654e761bfb15c43bfcf7ffeb6e3656d3b2772f6329d25d10f8062b3d809e","prov-2952b15a73b647e8f6f1909246540043a6642119eab2b8ddd292d8b989159e6e"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"wex-grievance","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","source":{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance","publisher":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu)","title":"Wex: grievance","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:06:18Z","content_sha256":"e342533040d64c8cbd8026a93163823f0bb1b9335d213da763466e14a1386af7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s5","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-5d64654e761bfb15c43bfcf7ffeb6e3656d3b2772f6329d25d10f8062b3d809e","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section5","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 5","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:36Z","content_sha256":"fdb248746b5c1acc6457f4d7f536ff00a6dd0bf3d5d9b7236f1b1e0e4f41ef78","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-petition-arb","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-2952b15a73b647e8f6f1909246540043a6642119eab2b8ddd292d8b989159e6e","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/file-a-petition-for-arbitration","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"File a petition for arbitration","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:21Z","content_sha256":"294a46c168513d79477f780146b893eced4d59a1b1aea5b0b0e6e8a21c27835a","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"def3bae7-569b-55d9-abee-e27badeebddd","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"How long do I have to file a grievance?","body":"It depends on your contract. The grievance procedure, including its time limits, is usually defined in the contract between the union and management, and deadlines differ from contract to contract. Contract time limits matter: when the Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (DLR) finds a union unlawfully refused to take a grievance to arbitration, its remedy is to order the union to ask the employer to waive the contract's arbitration time limits. A separate deadline applies to prohibited practice charges at the DLR: six months from when you knew or should have known. Read your contract's grievance article and tell your steward about the problem right away.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: grievance, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), F. Prohibited Practices, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/f-prohibited-practices)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-how-long-do-i-have-to-file-a-grievance","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-54b7f2b2dbc69b6446cc78eb611f84f73b8ed0aa8b9006b2216f99624c660621","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-how-long-do-i-have-to-file-a-grievance","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"How long do I have to file a grievance?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"3f2e381d79b9fdd7851d30fbb67d361eff4902ba9d95c7bfd7138c31e6d4d295","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","prov-ecae6940b308e391c248946ec43aa6ac002944d053d015fb9b902296489b0551"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-ulp-charge","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Public sector unfair labor practice charge","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:15Z","content_sha256":"a151c58def500412b27bc8f74f24865e90c2867a99c78cc29813dbb459e4c65f","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"wex-grievance","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","source":{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance","publisher":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu)","title":"Wex: grievance","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:06:18Z","content_sha256":"e342533040d64c8cbd8026a93163823f0bb1b9335d213da763466e14a1386af7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-f-prohibited","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-ecae6940b308e391c248946ec43aa6ac002944d053d015fb9b902296489b0551","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/f-prohibited-practices","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"F. Prohibited Practices","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:28Z","content_sha256":"f224cd36a7aed5e7970224b979c7bce2283f952dc3d88f3906e6f8873c11dfd5","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"4717b15f-a202-56a9-aaaf-0345aca1ab85","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Cuánto tiempo tengo para presentar una queja formal?","body":"Depende de su contrato. El procedimiento de quejas, incluidos sus plazos, normalmente está definido en el contrato entre el sindicato y la gerencia, y los plazos cambian de un contrato a otro. Los plazos del contrato importan: cuando el Departamento de Relaciones Laborales de Massachusetts (DLR) concluye que un sindicato se negó ilegalmente a llevar una queja a arbitraje, la solución que ordena es que el sindicato pida al empleador que renuncie a los plazos de arbitraje del contrato. Para los cargos por práctica prohibida ante el DLR hay un plazo distinto: seis meses desde que usted supo o debió saber del hecho. Lea el artículo de quejas de su contrato y avise de inmediato a su delegado o delegada sindical.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: grievance, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), F. Prohibited Practices, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/f-prohibited-practices)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-how-long-do-i-have-to-file-a-grievance","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-54b7f2b2dbc69b6446cc78eb611f84f73b8ed0aa8b9006b2216f99624c660621","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-how-long-do-i-have-to-file-a-grievance","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"How long do I have to file a grievance?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"3f2e381d79b9fdd7851d30fbb67d361eff4902ba9d95c7bfd7138c31e6d4d295","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","prov-ecae6940b308e391c248946ec43aa6ac002944d053d015fb9b902296489b0551"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-ulp-charge","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Public sector unfair labor practice charge","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:15Z","content_sha256":"a151c58def500412b27bc8f74f24865e90c2867a99c78cc29813dbb459e4c65f","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"wex-grievance","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","source":{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance","publisher":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu)","title":"Wex: grievance","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:06:18Z","content_sha256":"e342533040d64c8cbd8026a93163823f0bb1b9335d213da763466e14a1386af7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-f-prohibited","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-ecae6940b308e391c248946ec43aa6ac002944d053d015fb9b902296489b0551","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/f-prohibited-practices","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"F. Prohibited Practices","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:28Z","content_sha256":"f224cd36a7aed5e7970224b979c7bce2283f952dc3d88f3906e6f8873c11dfd5","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"cf6057ed-0426-549d-a341-849ed818d2e0","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What happens at each step of a grievance?","body":"Your contract sets the steps, who hears each one, and the deadlines. In general, a grievance procedure is a set of rules for documenting, presenting and resolving workplace disputes, and it may involve negotiation, mediation or arbitration. In Massachusetts public employment, a contract may include a procedure that ends in final and binding arbitration. The Department of Labor Relations (DLR) also offers grievance mediation, usually when the contract provides for it, though the parties may also agree to ask for it. A DLR grievance mediator tries to help both sides reach a voluntary settlement before arbitration. Ask your steward to walk you through the steps in your contract.","attribution":"","source":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), Wex: grievance, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/wex/grievance); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 8, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section8); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), C. Arbitration and Mediation Services, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/c-arbitration-and-mediation-services)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-happens-at-each-grievance-step","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-ec3e682f6790cb35a9da597e300f87ea10862e85507cc1baa5d305eeeba2f218","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-happens-at-each-grievance-step","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What happens at each step of a grievance?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"7b4719b25a5b3c7961e8dccf2808da895c0e96815f70b7b8f455ea26000e9b57","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-d3c11cdcb2fc2db731e8c3016853b534db924b729e8168353c3053d274ab68cd","prov-c4e88d90080bdab73b27a7cd4ea0379017407d40a749d99a3c94847982ef3c48","prov-28a7806565901ce7eb42c9a4b7bf47afe709c5ef6ea4283c5345f08424626c8d"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10