},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"lii-vaca","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-868f67459135ea084c824d90c025cab0fd25b5e7966b4ded0382d99040dd5749","source":{"url":"https://www.law.cornell.edu/supremecourt/text/386/171","publisher":"Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu)","title":"Vaca v. Sipes, 386 U.S. 171 (1967)","document_date":"1967-02-27"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:07:18Z","content_sha256":"165ea2a82bab9fec8b04580355af7dd8096102fa8bcf2b90410a069924d80c13","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"1967-02-27","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"b0dc6240-b0f4-531a-ad15-b1ad4c96cccb","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"Can I file a charge at the Department of Labor Relations myself? How long do I have?","body":"Yes. The Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (DLR) says a public employer, a union, or a person represented by a public-sector union can file an unfair labor practice charge, which c. 150E calls a prohibited practice. You must file within six months from the date you knew or should have known of the alleged violation. You can file online, by mail, or in person. The charge describes the alleged violation and names your employer and your union and their representatives, and you send a copy to the other side. The DLR then investigates. Your steward can help, but if the charge is against your union, you may want outside advice.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 11, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section11)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T15:19:13Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication. Code phase, 2026-10-12T15:19:13Z: Spanish question shortened from \"¿Cuánto tiempo tengo?\" to \"¿Qué plazo tengo?\" (same meaning) so it fits the learning editor's 100-character title; superseded record prov-53b193470c929d8178b7caa86020c57d073368a9d15338e29f026fdeb3ae3343.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-can-i-file-a-charge-at-the-dlr","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-bec00e8fd146dc17ebca8bc7064c39b2fa9735fa3dfc450c5af2f3c403869c24","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-can-i-file-a-charge-at-the-dlr","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"Can I file a charge at the Department of Labor Relations myself? How long do I have?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T15:19:13Z","content_sha256":"56211d3809929bfe04775f5c5cdf2f8bff8c871dd41c5438bdb633019c0ea9f6","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-d4990f7ba5c14c5bdad936818f6f8ca9730e5ee9d6e76caaf67c03a039b2ae7f"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T15:19:13Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication. Code phase, 2026-10-12T15:19:13Z: Spanish question shortened from \"¿Cuánto tiempo tengo?\" to \"¿Qué plazo tengo?\" (same meaning) so it fits the learning editor's 100-character title; superseded record prov-53b193470c929d8178b7caa86020c57d073368a9d15338e29f026fdeb3ae3343."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-ulp-charge","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Public sector unfair labor practice charge","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:15Z","content_sha256":"a151c58def500412b27bc8f74f24865e90c2867a99c78cc29813dbb459e4c65f","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s11","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-d4990f7ba5c14c5bdad936818f6f8ca9730e5ee9d6e76caaf67c03a039b2ae7f","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section11","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 11","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:46Z","content_sha256":"6ea055696317c50f44dc97d7259cefd302236184f44d5ac9d53fbdc50ac7436b","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"8f6b1697-991a-50db-a7db-4d5be53c9cb4","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Puedo presentar yo mismo un cargo ante el Departamento de Relaciones Laborales? ¿Qué plazo tengo?","body":"Sí. El Departamento de Relaciones Laborales de Massachusetts (DLR) dice que un empleador público, un sindicato o una persona representada por un sindicato del sector público puede presentar un cargo por práctica laboral injusta, que la ley c. 150E llama práctica prohibida. Debe presentarlo dentro de los seis meses desde la fecha en que supo o debió saber de la supuesta violación. Puede presentarlo en línea, por correo o en persona. El cargo describe la supuesta violación y nombra a su empleador y a su sindicato y a sus representantes, y usted envía una copia a la otra parte. Luego el DLR investiga. Su delegado o delegada sindical puede ayudarle, pero si el cargo es contra su sindicato, tal vez le convenga buscar asesoría externa.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 11, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section11)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T15:19:13Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication. Code phase, 2026-10-12T15:19:13Z: Spanish question shortened from \"¿Cuánto tiempo tengo?\" to \"¿Qué plazo tengo?\" (same meaning) so it fits the learning editor's 100-character title; superseded record prov-53b193470c929d8178b7caa86020c57d073368a9d15338e29f026fdeb3ae3343.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-can-i-file-a-charge-at-the-dlr","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-bec00e8fd146dc17ebca8bc7064c39b2fa9735fa3dfc450c5af2f3c403869c24","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-can-i-file-a-charge-at-the-dlr","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"Can I file a charge at the Department of Labor Relations myself? How long do I have?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T15:19:13Z","content_sha256":"56211d3809929bfe04775f5c5cdf2f8bff8c871dd41c5438bdb633019c0ea9f6","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-d4990f7ba5c14c5bdad936818f6f8ca9730e5ee9d6e76caaf67c03a039b2ae7f"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T15:19:13Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication. Code phase, 2026-10-12T15:19:13Z: Spanish question shortened from \"¿Cuánto tiempo tengo?\" to \"¿Qué plazo tengo?\" (same meaning) so it fits the learning editor's 100-character title; superseded record prov-53b193470c929d8178b7caa86020c57d073368a9d15338e29f026fdeb3ae3343."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-ulp-charge","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Public sector unfair labor practice charge","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:15Z","content_sha256":"a151c58def500412b27bc8f74f24865e90c2867a99c78cc29813dbb459e4c65f","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s11","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-d4990f7ba5c14c5bdad936818f6f8ca9730e5ee9d6e76caaf67c03a039b2ae7f","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section11","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 11","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:46Z","content_sha256":"6ea055696317c50f44dc97d7259cefd302236184f44d5ac9d53fbdc50ac7436b","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"83eed12c-5d33-5f45-af20-bfb1d32e3e4e","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"If I am fired or suspended, can I use both arbitration and a civil service appeal?","body":"Usually you must choose. Under c. 150E, s. 8, if you elect contract arbitration for a grievance about a suspension, dismissal, removal or termination, arbitration becomes the exclusive procedure, even if you would otherwise have rights under the civil service law (c. 31), the retirement law (c. 32), or the tenured teacher law (c. 71). The Department of Labor Relations (DLR) explains that for grievances on other issues, it may order binding arbitration even if the employee is pursuing other remedies. Because choosing one route can close another, talk with your steward before you file or appeal, and check the deadlines for each route.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 8, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section8); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), H. Final and Binding Grievance Arbitration, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/h-final-and-binding-grievance-arbitration)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-arbitration-or-civil-service","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-cdd55fb0c36b1ecef157625d23f560cd6f2c0cc0bb3544b6c2b794cc8abfeb8a","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-arbitration-or-civil-service","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"If I am fired or suspended, can I use both arbitration and a civil service appeal?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"a1cb82f18a91d9a919926ac81404bd6fa95c5e4bedd8c8748d3c3ec91db6bfc2","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-c4e88d90080bdab73b27a7cd4ea0379017407d40a749d99a3c94847982ef3c48","prov-1944ba533ef22375237609806374884c3e3da49fbc7672ef14440b8d33604a46"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"ma-150e-s8","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-c4e88d90080bdab73b27a7cd4ea0379017407d40a749d99a3c94847982ef3c48","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section8","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 8","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:41Z","content_sha256":"d35cfe7426c0d1815be725457582e2337b3ebf9a24fb26b4f880b7cd19a659c7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-h-grievance-arb","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-1944ba533ef22375237609806374884c3e3da49fbc7672ef14440b8d33604a46","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/h-final-and-binding-grievance-arbitration","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"H. Final and Binding Grievance Arbitration","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:17Z","content_sha256":"2aa806bba71921a56759bf0c7f84b65e932250eae583c4261202c5140e9cafe7","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"392be721-3bd4-5508-a002-43d16a913120","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"Si me despiden o suspenden, ¿puedo usar tanto el arbitraje como una apelación de servicio civil?","body":"Normalmente debe elegir. Según la ley c. 150E, sección 8, si usted elige el arbitraje del contrato para una queja sobre una suspensión, despido, destitución o terminación, el arbitraje pasa a ser el único procedimiento, aunque de otro modo tuviera derechos según la ley de servicio civil (c. 31), la ley de jubilación (c. 32) o la ley de maestros con permanencia (c. 71). El Departamento de Relaciones Laborales (DLR) explica que, para quejas sobre otros temas, puede ordenar arbitraje obligatorio aunque el empleado esté usando otras vías. Como elegir una vía puede cerrar otra, hable con su delegado o delegada sindical antes de presentar una queja o una apelación, y revise los plazos de cada vía.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 8, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section8); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), H. Final and Binding Grievance Arbitration, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/h-final-and-binding-grievance-arbitration)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","grievances"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-arbitration-or-civil-service","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-cdd55fb0c36b1ecef157625d23f560cd6f2c0cc0bb3544b6c2b794cc8abfeb8a","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-arbitration-or-civil-service","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"If I am fired or suspended, can I use both arbitration and a civil service appeal?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"a1cb82f18a91d9a919926ac81404bd6fa95c5e4bedd8c8748d3c3ec91db6bfc2","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-c4e88d90080bdab73b27a7cd4ea0379017407d40a749d99a3c94847982ef3c48","prov-1944ba533ef22375237609806374884c3e3da49fbc7672ef14440b8d33604a46"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"ma-150e-s8","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-c4e88d90080bdab73b27a7cd4ea0379017407d40a749d99a3c94847982ef3c48","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section8","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 8","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:41Z","content_sha256":"d35cfe7426c0d1815be725457582e2337b3ebf9a24fb26b4f880b7cd19a659c7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-h-grievance-arb","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-1944ba533ef22375237609806374884c3e3da49fbc7672ef14440b8d33604a46","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/h-final-and-binding-grievance-arbitration","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"H. Final and Binding Grievance Arbitration","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:17Z","content_sha256":"2aa806bba71921a56759bf0c7f84b65e932250eae583c4261202c5140e9cafe7","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"89d61986-5af2-5758-a48d-32fa785c8525","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"How is a contract negotiated?","body":"In Massachusetts public employment, c. 150E, s. 6 requires the employer and the union that is the exclusive representative to meet at reasonable times, including before the employer's budget process, and to negotiate in good faith about wages, hours, standards of productivity and performance, and other terms and conditions of employment. Neither side is forced to agree to a proposal or make a concession, but both must bargain in good faith to agreement or impasse. Each side picks its own representatives for the table. If they reach agreement, it is put in writing, signed by the parties, and filed with the state. Your steward can tell you how your union keeps members informed.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - The Collective Bargaining Process, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-the-collective-bargaining-process); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 6, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section6); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-how-is-a-contract-negotiated","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-8815883e569c6e813023f00ef7e208a859081c8365ea3747f759dc2744a68e9a","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-how-is-a-contract-negotiated","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"How is a contract negotiated?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"731bc7ef0b9d9a9c9b010e993c344239c1c3a61fd262982c5950b613958183af","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8f25653210c21b4f2f69e663cae59958605f80c446cafebdabfecc5112ab98c1","prov-abe559051ea5e8f918504248d398caf1aeace3bb9c52271faa8dc41da1f00323","prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-faq-bargaining","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8f25653210c21b4f2f69e663cae59958605f80c446cafebdabfecc5112ab98c1","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-the-collective-bargaining-process","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"FAQ - The Collective Bargaining Process","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:55Z","content_sha256":"22163b7c777bcbf7dd11ecd7d0bc918fe247e366a1f2eea23316079bf7c1ed8b","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s6","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-abe559051ea5e8f918504248d398caf1aeace3bb9c52271faa8dc41da1f00323","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section6","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 6","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:38Z","content_sha256":"4dccd774006ead9f4b85112c6d01ea8bb46e3c162d1db0ebd799c096b5fa0e54","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s7","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:39Z","content_sha256":"79bd21e29442b6264292d5e9ab5b8c01075862c03bd3ac24ad0daa34520f21d7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"8457bdbe-c37e-58ca-a235-fc5eef7ebae8","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Cómo se negocia un convenio colectivo (contrato)?","body":"En el empleo público de Massachusetts, la ley c. 150E, sección 6, exige que el empleador y el sindicato que es el representante exclusivo se reúnan en momentos razonables, incluso antes del proceso de presupuesto del empleador, y negocien de buena fe sobre salarios, horarios, normas de productividad y desempeño, y otros términos y condiciones de empleo. Ninguna parte está obligada a aceptar una propuesta ni a hacer una concesión, pero ambas deben negociar de buena fe hasta llegar a un acuerdo o a un impasse (estancamiento). Cada parte elige a sus propios representantes en la mesa. Si llegan a un acuerdo, se pone por escrito, lo firman las partes y se presenta ante el estado. Su delegado o delegada sindical puede decirle cómo su sindicato mantiene informados a los miembros.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - The Collective Bargaining Process, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-the-collective-bargaining-process); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 6, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section6); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"con