tent reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"b9382228-75b7-5aa1-a5da-569b1d233949","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What happens when my contract expires?","body":"It depends partly on your contract. Under c. 150E, s. 7, a contract may say its terms stay in effect after three years until a successor agreement is negotiated. Bargaining for the next contract continues either way. Once either side files a petition with the Department of Labor Relations (DLR) for an impasse determination in successor talks, s. 9 says the employer may not make unilateral changes, and the existing terms and conditions continue until the bargaining process, including mediation and fact-finding, is complete. The DLR also says the law prohibits public employers from unilaterally changing terms and conditions of employment. Ask your steward what your contract says about expiration.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - Impasse, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-happens-when-the-contract-expires","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-522d95d030757d30bcebb145e4ef183ec33de9b07d4b9bb52709e26594a61d15","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-happens-when-the-contract-expires","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What happens when my contract expires?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"b2c1aacc4e0b4b8e4e03c658a4681726c2dd79029565c67891e41ff14efc5f9f","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-862a8a6354312a6c232dba0a4760d6259b033ed25277377cca373a893b11db8b","prov-e35a27fdde2fe7d3a13b665cb6fbd0387053211e82ef5dbc61cd7dd15e151778","prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"ma-150e-s9","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-862a8a6354312a6c232dba0a4760d6259b033ed25277377cca373a893b11db8b","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:42Z","content_sha256":"20ec3b4addae50fa6ec627035a8950581bf115e5974661adc1b22414016851ef","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-faq-impasse","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-e35a27fdde2fe7d3a13b665cb6fbd0387053211e82ef5dbc61cd7dd15e151778","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"FAQ - Impasse","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:04Z","content_sha256":"29cb41bf93f0dc9cbeac6c370763eb7ef4a891dba5977069306e282accddc82e","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s7","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:39Z","content_sha256":"79bd21e29442b6264292d5e9ab5b8c01075862c03bd3ac24ad0daa34520f21d7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"4e3df47b-29ed-5ee5-af0d-636fa90a2109","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Qué pasa cuando vence mi contrato?","body":"Depende en parte de su contrato. Según la ley c. 150E, sección 7, un contrato puede decir que sus términos siguen vigentes después de tres años hasta que se negocie un acuerdo sucesor. La negociación del siguiente contrato continúa en cualquier caso. Cuando una de las partes presenta ante el Departamento de Relaciones Laborales (DLR) una petición para declarar un impasse (estancamiento) en la negociación de un acuerdo sucesor, la sección 9 dice que el empleador no puede hacer cambios unilaterales, y los términos y condiciones vigentes continúan hasta que termine el proceso de negociación, incluidos la mediación y la determinación de hechos (fact-finding). El DLR también dice que la ley prohíbe a los empleadores públicos cambiar unilateralmente los términos y condiciones de empleo. Pregunte a su delegado o delegada sindical qué dice su contrato sobre el vencimiento.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - Impasse, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-happens-when-the-contract-expires","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-522d95d030757d30bcebb145e4ef183ec33de9b07d4b9bb52709e26594a61d15","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-happens-when-the-contract-expires","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What happens when my contract expires?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"b2c1aacc4e0b4b8e4e03c658a4681726c2dd79029565c67891e41ff14efc5f9f","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-862a8a6354312a6c232dba0a4760d6259b033ed25277377cca373a893b11db8b","prov-e35a27fdde2fe7d3a13b665cb6fbd0387053211e82ef5dbc61cd7dd15e151778","prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"ma-150e-s9","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-862a8a6354312a6c232dba0a4760d6259b033ed25277377cca373a893b11db8b","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:42Z","content_sha256":"20ec3b4addae50fa6ec627035a8950581bf115e5974661adc1b22414016851ef","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-faq-impasse","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-e35a27fdde2fe7d3a13b665cb6fbd0387053211e82ef5dbc61cd7dd15e151778","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"FAQ - Impasse","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:04Z","content_sha256":"29cb41bf93f0dc9cbeac6c370763eb7ef4a891dba5977069306e282accddc82e","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s7","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:39Z","content_sha256":"79bd21e29442b6264292d5e9ab5b8c01075862c03bd3ac24ad0daa34520f21d7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"495c2ec5-9908-5f0d-a9ac-2b87978f7877","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What is impasse, and what happens next?","body":"Impasse means negotiations are stuck. In Massachusetts public employment, after a reasonable period of bargaining, either side or both may ask the Department of Labor Relations (DLR) to decide whether an impasse exists. If it does, the DLR appoints a mediator, or the parties pick one. If mediation fails, either side may ask for fact-finding: a neutral fact-finder holds a hearing and writes a report with recommendations. Those recommendations are advisory and do not bind the parties, and the DLR makes them public if the impasse is still unresolved ten days later. Only after the DLR certifies that the process is complete may the employer put in place its last best final offer. Police and fire bargaining uses a separate committee (JLMC).","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - Impasse, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse); 