quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-fact-finding","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-f067825e2b4b91770b0f52b9b36de83af69bf196f52615093169920d3202e25a","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/fact-finding","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Fact-finding","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:08Z","content_sha256":"9d9bb5ef9e003f27885245296edfde1e2e55f0bfed1e632c79033627c6fd74ac","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-g-impasse","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-9904013c32f8f6e188c5eb1da439acb4261f6c606407c8482dd5c91df3dc65cb","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/g-impasse","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"G. Impasse","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:13Z","content_sha256":"bafbe47fd1f144355ba80ba959b1fff1e28c9a016ac45c2c82c8d4f2667afb7b","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"b2cad702-855e-512e-a2ad-e9ea8d4506f8","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Qué es un impasse y qué pasa después?","body":"Un impasse (estancamiento) significa que la negociación está trabada. En el empleo público de Massachusetts, después de un período razonable de negociación, una de las partes o ambas pueden pedir al Departamento de Relaciones Laborales (DLR) que decida si existe un impasse. Si existe, el DLR nombra un mediador, o las partes eligen uno. Si la mediación (mediation) fracasa, cualquiera de las partes puede pedir la determinación de hechos (fact-finding): una persona neutral celebra una audiencia y escribe un informe con recomendaciones. Esas recomendaciones son consultivas y no obligan a las partes, y el DLR las hace públicas si el impasse sigue sin resolverse diez días después. Solo después de que el DLR certifica que el proceso terminó puede el empleador aplicar su última y mejor oferta final. La negociación de policías y bomberos usa un comité aparte (JLMC).","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - Impasse, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Fact-finding, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/fact-finding); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), G. Impasse, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/g-impasse)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not 