:{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-g-impasse","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-9904013c32f8f6e188c5eb1da439acb4261f6c606407c8482dd5c91df3dc65cb","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/g-impasse","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"G. Impasse","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:13Z","content_sha256":"bafbe47fd1f144355ba80ba959b1fff1e28c9a016ac45c2c82c8d4f2667afb7b","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"56f78e19-2716-5b1b-a4a9-dd1d507bc1bf","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"Can public employees in Massachusetts strike?","body":"No. Under c. 150E, s. 9A, no public employee or employee organization may strike, or induce, encourage or condone a strike, work stoppage, slowdown or withholding of services. If a strike occurs or is about to occur, the employer petitions the state to investigate, and enforcement can go to superior court. Under s. 15, employees are not paid for strike days and may face discipline and discharge. The law's definition of strike still protects your right to express a complaint or opinion about working conditions. Private-sector workers have a right to strike under the NLRA, with many limits. Ask your steward before joining any job action.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 15, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section15); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 9A, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section9A); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 1, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section1); National Labor Relations Board (nlrb.gov), The NLRA and the Right to Strike, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.nlrb.gov/about-nlrb/rights-we-protect/your-rights/nlra-and-the-right-to-strike)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-can-public-employees-strike-in-massachusetts","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-61489d5488b41c6f6f22d62c936264fe77edb58bc4a98127a80ce2d51cfdbfc9","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-can-public-employees-strike-in-massachusetts","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"Can public employees in Massachusetts strike?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"5d39e5bc4a58749d944