eXXI/Chapter150E/Section7","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:39Z","content_sha256":"79bd21e29442b6264292d5e9ab5b8c01075862c03bd3ac24ad0daa34520f21d7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"ef3409ee-8a4a-544d-adb4-9a272ba5bfee","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What is ratification, and do I get a vote?","body":"Ratification is the step in which contract terms are approved under the union's own procedures. Whether members vote, who may vote, and how, depends on your union's constitution and bylaws. Unions covered by the federal Labor-Management Reporting and Disclosure Act (LMRDA) must file a statement with the U.S. Department of Labor describing how contract terms are ratified, and those filings can be searched in the OLMS Online Public Disclosure Room. In Massachusetts public employment, once an agreement is reached it is put in writing, signed by the parties, and filed with the state. Ask your steward or union office for the ratification rules that apply to you.","attribution":"","source":"U.S. Department of Labor, Office of Labor-Management Standards (dol.gov), OLMS Online Public Disclosure Room, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.dol.gov/agencies/olms/public-disclosure-room); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 431 - Report of labor organizations, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/431); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-is-ratification-do-i-vote","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-a0ac6a92c0d400455488acedc51a95e3783ac5a41cbb7ba9ae6c8479c2cc2802","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-is-ratification-do-i-vote","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What is ratification, and do I get a vote?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"c480134c2dce0b97443fabc34bb0f790ce89b14026bfecd83541f0f326d9b0c7","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-e137149bcb356d90f11b97116b55a2665e46357345e9b01e3e737449045ca86d","prov-c7bfdf0c8b0ca70089e10fd447440bd95248d9e18bebf53e00f3ef20d903f99f","prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against