{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s7","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-9ff70d90b04e4d4b84d074f2379281256c7d263dd1786e950bee8180dc12ab6c","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:39Z","content_sha256":"79bd21e29442b6264292d5e9ab5b8c01075862c03bd3ac24ad0daa34520f21d7","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"b0701210-e4d2-54ac-a702-066529965f54","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Qué es la ratificación y tengo derecho a votar?","body":"La ratificación es el paso en el que se aprueban los términos del contrato según los procedimientos propios del sindicato. Si los miembros votan, quién puede votar y cómo, depende de la constitución y los estatutos de su sindicato. Los sindicatos cubiertos por la ley federal Labor-Management Reporting and Disclosure Act (LMRDA) deben presentar ante el Departamento de Trabajo de EE. UU. una declaración que explique cómo se ratifican los términos del contrato, y esos documentos se pueden buscar en la Sala de Divulgación Pública en línea de la OLMS. En el empleo público de Massachusetts, cuando se llega a un acuerdo, se pone por escrito, lo firman las partes y se presenta ante el estado. Pida a su delegado o delegada sindical o a la oficina del sindicato las reglas de ratificación que le aplican.","attribution":"","source":"U.S. Department of Labor, Office of Labor-Management Standards (dol.gov), OLMS Online Public Disclosure Room, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.dol.gov/agencies/olms/public-disclosure-room); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 431 - Report of labor organizations, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/431); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 7, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section7)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","bargaining"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-is-ratification-do-i-vote","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-a0ac6a92c0d400455488acedc51a95e3783ac5a41cbb7ba9ae6c8479c2cc2802","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-is-ratification-do-i-vote","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What is ratification, and do I get a vote?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"c480134c2dce0b97443fabc34bb0f790ce89b14026bfecd83541f0f326d9b0c7","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-e13