ointed by the governor. Under state law it includes a dispute resolution office, an advisory council, the Commonwealth Employment Relations Board (CERB), and the Joint Labor-Management Committee for police and fire. A State Auditor's report says most of its work is deciding prohibited practice charges under c. 150E for public employees and c. 150A for some private employers. It also runs elections, mediation, fact-finding and grievance arbitration. It has offices in Boston, Springfield and Worcester.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 23, section 9O (Department of Labor Relations), retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleII/Chapter23/Section9O); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - Impasse, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-impasse); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), File a petition for arbitration, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/file-a-petition-for-arbitration); Massachusetts Office of the State Auditor (mass.gov), Audit of the Department of Labor Relations: overview of the Department of Labor Relations, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/overview-of-the-department-of-labor-relations)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required 