":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"dlr-overview","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-fe5f61dd7efae0ca8e4dc592e00f979fd4a5dba14ea2a585ca58e53bfd36d7e6","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/overview-of-the-department-of-labor-relations","publisher":"Massachusetts Office of the State Auditor (mass.gov)","title":"Audit of the Department of Labor Relations: overview of the Department of Labor Relations","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:08:58Z","content_sha256":"e70c1467eda23a7d338698577fc3b5005d7b2ec4318c6b29ede254be9e6d1e8e","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"644aa8ec-ed10-568f-aaf5-592355cb7ac4","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"What is the Commonwealth Employment Relations Board (CERB)?","body":"The Commonwealth Employment Relations Board (CERB) is the three-member appeals board inside the Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (DLR). It has one full-time chair and two per-diem members, appointed by the governor from names sent by the DLR's advisory council, for five-year terms, and no more than two may be from the same political party. The CERB decides appeals of dismissed prohibited practice charges and of hearing officer decisions, and it also decides appropriate bargaining units in some cases. A hearing officer's order becomes final unless a party asks the CERB to review it within 10 days. A final CERB order can be appealed to the Appeals Court within 30 days.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 23, section 9R (Commonwealth Employment Relations Board), retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleII/Chapter23/Section9R); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), FAQ - General Information, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/faq-general-information); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 11, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section11)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","the-board"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-is-the-cerb","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-c72283a4221f1c316c09414878de45118f3f230f54646a3dcfd2d755aa616a40","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-is-the-cerb","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What is the Commonwealth Employment Relations Board (CERB)?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"f003f013e65005810ba6612a75be9bdd1d1b61198128ceae2a25ad7e8fb65fd9","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-11299a412c78