e":"What is a prohibited practice?","body":"\"Prohibited practice\" is the Massachusetts public-sector term for what federal law calls an unfair labor practice. Under c. 150E, s. 10, an employer may not interfere with, restrain or coerce employees in using their rights; dominate or interfere with a union; discriminate to encourage or discourage union membership; retaliate against an employee for filing a complaint or giving testimony; refuse to bargain in good faith; or refuse to take part in good faith in mediation, fact-finding and arbitration. A union may not interfere with, restrain or coerce employees or employers, refuse to bargain in good faith, or refuse to take part in those procedures. Charges go to the Department of Labor Relations (DLR) within six months.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 10, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section10)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","the-board"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-is-a-prohibited-practice","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-938b7c0075eebd6fda225e32ce7a17b8db28267fd7f944734a472508b845d7e8","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-is-a-prohibited-practice","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What is a prohibited practice?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"44c070d4f4025b05c4f11a459319ed0da01e549ef7a1cb7006eacafe0c36062f","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-2c059c955d72c4c595e3f43bc0687c642ae14534a28bd6775c9da73615b1639b"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-ulp-charge","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Public sector unfair labor practice charge","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:15Z","content_sha256":"a151c58def500412b27bc8f74f24865e90c2867a99c78cc29813dbb459e4c65f","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s10","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-2c059c955d72c4c595e3f43bc0687c642ae14534a28bd6775c9da73615b1639b","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section10","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 10","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:45Z","content_sha256":"666745eb1ada7ab2249397939fb9f0de5e86cf19bc5d3612ae8072618feec42d","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"e4505132-d8fd-55ed-a909-d8f157ff449f","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"es","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"¿Qué es una práctica prohibida?","body":"\"Práctica prohibida\" (prohibited practice) es el término del sector público de Massachusetts para lo que la ley federal llama práctica laboral injusta (unfair labor practice). Según la ley c. 150E, sección 10, un empleador no puede interferir, restringir ni presionar a los empleados en el uso de sus derechos; dominar o interferir con un sindicato; discriminar para fomentar o desalentar la afiliación sindical; tomar represalias contra un empleado por presentar una queja o dar testimonio; negarse a negociar de buena fe; ni negarse a participar de buena fe en la mediación, la determinación de hechos y el arbitraje. Un sindicato no puede interferir, restringir ni presionar a empleados o empleadores, negarse a negociar de buena fe ni negarse a participar en esos procedimientos. Los cargos se presentan ante el Departamento de Relaciones Laborales (DLR) dentro de los seis meses.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 10, consultada el 12 oct 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section10)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","the-board"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-what-is-a-prohibited-practice","locale":"es","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-938b7c0075eebd6fda225e32ce7a17b8db28267fd7f944734a472508b845d7e8","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-what-is-a-prohibited-practice","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"What is a prohibited practice?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"44c070d4f4025b05c4f11a459319ed0da01e549ef7a1cb7006eacafe0c36062f","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-2c059c955d72c4c595e3f43bc0687c642ae14534a28bd6775c9da73615b1639b"],"review":{"status":"reviewed","reviewed_at":"2026-10-12T07:41:37Z","reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":"Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication."},"reuse":{"basis":"owner-authored","note":"Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only."}},"source_records":[{"source_key":"dlr-ulp-charge","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","source":{"url":"https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge","publisher":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov)","title":"Public sector unfair labor practice charge","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:09:15Z","content_sha256":"a151c58def500412b27bc8f74f24865e90c2867a99c78cc29813dbb459e4c65f","capture":{"method":"firecrawl"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}},{"source_key":"ma-150e-s10","provenance":{"provenance_id":"prov-2c059c955d72c4c595e3f43bc0687c642ae14534a28bd6775c9da73615b1639b","source":{"url":"https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section10","publisher":"Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov)","title":"M.G.L. c. 150E, section 10","document_date":null},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:04:45Z","content_sha256":"666745eb1ada7ab2249397939fb9f0de5e86cf19bc5d3612ae8072618feec42d","capture":{"method":"http-get"},"extraction":{"method":"verbatim","extractor":"public source capture text view","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":[],"review":{"status":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"0a5d7dbc-7a30-54ad-af0e-9e9ab2a2a485","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"Do I go to the DLR or the NLRB?","body":"It depends on your employer. If you work for the state, a county, a city or town, or another Massachusetts public employer, your labor rights come from c. 150E and charges go to the Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (DLR). The National Labor Relations Act does not cover state or local government employers. The National Labor Relations Board (NLRB) is the federal agency for most private-sector workers, and its jurisdiction covers the great majority of non-government employers. Some private-sector employers, unions or represented workers may be able to file with the DLR instead. If you are not sure, ask your steward or contact either agency.","attribution":"","source":"Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), Public sector unfair labor practice charge, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/how-to/public-sector-unfair-labor-practice-charge); Massachusetts Trial Court Law Libraries (mass.gov), Massachusetts law about unions and collective bargaining, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/massachusetts-law-about-unions-and-collective-bargaining); Legal Information Institute, Cornell Law School (law.cornell.edu), 29 U.S. Code 152 - Definitions (NLRA), retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.law.cornell.edu/uscode/text/29/152); Massachusetts General Court (malegislature.gov), M.G.L. c. 150E, section 1, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://malegislature.gov/Laws/GeneralLaws/PartI/TitleXXI/Chapter150E/Section1); National Labor Relations Board (nlrb.gov), Jurisdictional Standards, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.nlrb.gov/about-nlrb/rights-we-protect/the-law/jurisdictional-standards)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","the-board"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance":{"content_path":"content/explainer-content/faq.json","unit_id":"faq-dlr-or-nlrb","locale":"en","record":{"provenance_id":"prov-81d8cab01193530c917a80b46d71449daaaac55a67fb97777e935d386c30001a","source":{"url":"https://app.example.invalid/#faq-dlr-or-nlrb","publisher":"Union Ground platform content (authored draft)","title":"Do I go to the DLR or the NLRB?","document_date":"2026-10-12"},"retrieved_at":"2026-10-12T07:42:08Z","content_sha256":"53595db1ee5fa3ef87a355eaf90c91f860d0a078f9ed7ffcdce2a8548e74de42","capture":{"method":"authored"},"extraction":{"method":"model","extractor":"bilingual draft generation, en+es; quotes checked by quotation validation","quote_binding":"exact-substring"},"as_of":"2026-10-12","derived_from":["prov-8d886c64c852c30ba3c7840a80cd711d7fc31ef373b36ab5b1511b79f411d254","prov-aff405b89ac74f989f8502acd0a86d06d0174a84cc5f71d7d251720ce8097e3b","prov-12171ec99baffa229634d78d17382025affed91de92a3f43a6893ea0faa9e051","prov-946c243f5c2e016d2c7cca739060f56da00c7fdffa96b123a14c06623d3d