tatus":"unreviewed","reviewed_at":null,"reviewer_role":"content reviewer","note":""},"reuse":{"basis":"public-record","note":"Cited and paraphrased; not republished in full."}}}]}},{"id":"4e02dc39-2bc5-5dfe-aa5c-267e8f9bcda8","payload":{"kind":"mini_lesson","locale":"en","locale_state":"reviewed","title":"Is this legal advice?","body":"No. This app gives general information about labor law and how it usually works. It is not legal advice, and it cannot account for the facts of your situation or the exact words of your contract. Even government guidance says this: the Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations notes that its Janus Q&A does not carry the force of law and is not a substitute for advice from your own legal counsel. For questions about your own job, start with your steward. For legal questions, such as a possible lawsuit or criminal charge, talk with a lawyer.","attribution":"","source":"National Labor Relations Board (nlrb.gov), The NLRA and the Right to Strike, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.nlrb.gov/about-nlrb/rights-we-protect/your-rights/nlra-and-the-right-to-strike); Massachusetts Department of Labor Relations (mass.gov), DLR Q&A re: Janus v. AFSCME, retrieved Oct 12, 2026 (https://www.mass.gov/info-details/dlr-qa-re-janus-v-american-fed-of-state-cty-muni-employees)","rights_note":"owner-authored: Original plain-language text drafted for the platform; statutes, regulations, agency pages and court opinions are cited and paraphrased, short quotations only.","review_note":"source review, 2026-10-12T07:41:37Z: Fresh-context verification pass: every claim read against its verbatim source quotes in context, Spanish checked against English, jurisdiction and affiliation guardrails checked. Not yet reviewed by the platform editor; editor review is required before publication.","bullets":[],"direction":"","topics":["faq","using-the-app"],"audience":"all","tone":"","learning_outcome":"","factual_claims":true,"priority":0,"is_default":false},"provenance"